---
description: Testing and evaluation conventions
globs: tests/**/*
---
- **Unit test structure**: use `# Arrange`, `# Act`, `# Assert` comments in Python `tests/unittest` and UI `*.test.ts(x)` files (combined lines OK for one-liners)
- **Eval**: `make -C tests/eval run-retrieval-suite` → `python tests/retrieval/main.py` (pydantic-evals `Dataset.evaluate()`, running api, same event loop as the HTTP client); `make -C tests/eval run-generation-suite` → `python tests/generation/main.py` (DeepEval `evaluate()`, running stack). Each live suite has `settings.py` next to the runner. Goldens in `dataset-investigation.json` (live) and `dataset.json` (offline unittest)
- **Repo map drift**: structural changes must update root `project.cue` and pass `make verify-repo-map` ([ADR 008](../docs/adr/008-repo-metadata-in-cue.md))
- **In-service tests are unit only** (no `tests/integration/` under services) — HTTP acceptance is `tests/api`; see [ADR 004](../docs/adr/004-no-in-service-integration-tests.md)
- **Default CI is unit-only** — no docker-compose, `tests/api`, `tests/e2e`, or `eval-live`; see [ADR 007](../docs/adr/007-no-live-tests-in-ci.md) (demo/reference project, not production revenue software)
- API Gherkin (`tests/api`): Playwright-BDD against live api/chat/admin; steps use **only** clients generated from `openapi/*.yaml`; `make api-test`; manual / on-demand
- Eval layout: `src/agentic_eval/core/` is a light settings abstraction (`CoreSettings`: OpenAI-compatible LiteLLM key + tenant + published api/chat URLs + `eval_env_file()`). `core/clients/` composes generated OpenAPI clients (`ChatHttp` / `ApiHttp`); SSE frame parse lives next to them because the generator returns a string body. Custom DeepEval `BaseMetric` extensions live in `core/deepeval/metrics.py` (Required Phrases, Abstention); `core/deepeval/evaluate.py` wraps DeepEval `evaluate()` (markdown under `reports/eval/`). Custom pydantic-evals `Evaluator` extensions live in `core/pydantic_evals/metrics.py` (`RetrievalIR`); `core/pydantic_evals/evaluate.py` wraps `Dataset.evaluate()` + `report.print()`. Retrieval IR calls `POST /v1/retrieval/search` on the running api. `core/golden/` loads and validates goldens (`GoldenDataset`, `LabeledGolden`, `AbstentionGolden`). Suite gates are **not** in src — `tests/generation/settings.py` and `tests/retrieval/settings.py` sit next to the runners. pytest: `tests/unittest/` offline; live suites are `tests/retrieval/main.py` and `tests/generation/main.py`. Retrieval ranking is not DeepEval contextual precision/recall
- Goldens are grounded in `resources/` PDFs (not the repo itself). Typed as `LabeledGolden | AbstentionGolden`. Tier 1 IR: document Recall@k, chunk Precision@k, Hit Rate@k, MRR, nDCG@k on labeled `expected_source_file` / `expected_source_files`. Tier 2 generation: labeled goldens in one DeepEval `evaluate()` call (Faithfulness / Answer Relevancy, one progress bar); abstention goldens in a second `evaluate()` with `AbstentionMetric` only — judge via LiteLLM `judge` alias (`EVAL_JUDGE_MODEL`), not the `generate` model. SUT fan-out is `EVAL_MAX_CONCURRENCY` (default 20). Judge is serial: `EVAL_JUDGE_MAX_CONCURRENCY` (default 1), `EVAL_JUDGE_THROTTLE_SECONDS` (default 2), metrics `async_mode=False`. `EVAL_JUDGE_RETRY_*` (defaults 10 / 2s / 60s cap) is written onto DeepEval's live Settings singleton (not `os.environ`) so gpt-4o 429s are not quality FAILs under LiteLLM `rpm: 30`. DeepEval writes timestamped markdown under `reports/eval/` — not gitignored `.reports/`
- Eval config is `CoreSettings` (`EVAL_` prefix: tenant, OpenAI-compatible key/URL, `EVAL_CHAT_URL` / `EVAL_API_URL` with `EVAL_SUT_*` aliases). Live suites talk to api/chat over HTTP — not Qdrant, not in-process LangGraph. Suites load `tests/eval/.env` via pydantic-settings (copy `.env.example`; do not `source` it — bash mangles JSON). Proxy bearer aliases: `EVAL_OPENAI_API_KEY` / `EVAL_SUT_LITELLM_API_KEY` / `LITELLM_MASTER_KEY` / `OPENAI_API_KEY`; empty values are ignored.
- **LangSmith** prod tracing: `LANGSMITH_ENABLED=true` on chat service (LangGraph auto-traces)
- Quality recipes: `tools/qa` (`unittest`, `system-test` = all measuring suites, `license`, `eval-live`, `e2e`); included from the root Makefile
- E2E UI: `tests/e2e` (Playwright + Gherkin); not in default CI; `make -C tests/e2e run-smoke-suite` (`@smoke`), `run-regression-suite` (`@regression`), `run` = both. `npm run test:demo` for slow human-like video
